{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nA sidecar payload is keyed by `(change_id, revision)` (`sidecar.py:99-101`) and Gerrit emits one\n`code_review` artifact per revision (`review_bot/artifact_emit.py:84`), so a finding raised on one\npatchset and not re-emitted on the next reaches no consumer. On change 1867 the `assert elapsed < 10`\nadvisory ran on PS1-PS2 and vanished on PS3-PS4, which merged `LLM-Review+1` with zero findings; the\ndefect then broke macOS CI on 1869 (bug `9bb7-4430-1202-4d93`). Recall is non-deterministic per run.\nApproved 2026-08-21.\n\nMemory exists but only NARROWS: `apply_region_gated_floor` (`workflow_ops.py:641`) reads\n`latest_code_review_result` (`sidecar.py:354`) to drop findings, never to re-raise one.\n\n## Approach\n\nMirror plan-review's recall backstop (`plan_review/sidecar.py:414-495`, injected at `pass1.py:489`) —\nno second mechanism. Paths omit `src/rebar/`.\n\n- **Where state is computed.** New leaf `llm/code_review/carry_forward.py`. `standing_items(key, *,\n  repo_root, coverage=None)` reads the prior payload via `latest_code_review_result` (extended to\n  also return `revision`, so each item knows its origin patchset) and classifies each item with\n  `region_gate.region_for_finding(f, prior_deps, repo_root=…)` (`region_gate.py:31`) against that\n  payload's `deps` content-hash map. Classification lives HERE, not in `merge_findings`\n  (`workflow_ops.py:237`), which sees only finding lists and has no deps/region access; merge gets\n  resolved items as data.\n- **Eligibility.** Surfaced-only — the reader unions `blocking` + `advisory` only and\n  `standing_items` must NOT widen that, or findings the floor permanently dropped come back (bug\n  `old-frilly-plankton`). Grounded-only — empty `evidence` is ineligible: the verifier has nothing\n  to re-ground, so it would confirm a bare assertion (bug `deceitful-flannel-jerboa`). Highest\n  `priority` first, capped at `STANDING_CAP = 12` (plan-review's `RECALL_CAP`, `sidecar.py:368`).\n- **State — one rule per value**, on a new additive `standing` sub-object `{origin_revision,\n  origin_decision, state}` (no `disposition` field exists today):\n  - `still-present` — cited file's current hash == the prior review's (`REGION_UNCHANGED`), or the\n    signal is unresolvable (`REGION_UNKNOWN`: multi-file, absent path, error). CARRIED. UNKNOWN\n    defaults here deliberately: the clamp below means carrying can only lower a posture.\n  - `addressed` — cited file's content differs (`REGION_CHANGED`): the edit is evidence it was acted\n    on, so the fresh finder's silence rules. NOT carried.\n  - `withdrawn` — the prior item ITSELF carries a `standing` object: already carried once. NOT\n    carried.\n  Example: PS2 raises `security` at `a.py:40`; PS3 leaves `a.py` byte-identical and does not re-emit\n  it → `still-present`, injected into PS3. PS4 edits `a.py` → `addressed`. Had PS4 left it untouched\n  and still missed it, PS3's carried item is `withdrawn`.\n- **Termination (anti-ratchet).** plan-review suppresses recall wholesale on changed material\n  (`_material_changed`, `sidecar.py:396`); `addressed` is the per-finding analogue and `withdrawn`\n  bounds the rest — an item is carried AT MOST ONCE, so the chain ends after one patchset even\n  if its region churns. Per-state counts land in `coverage`.\n- **Injection point.** Pass-1 assembly, NOT `finalize.py` (its docstring `:1-9`: post-verdict only).\n  Items resolve in `gate_dispatch._assemble_code_review_run` (`:401` — the only site holding\n  `session_id`/`change_id`; keyed `session:<id>` local / `change:<id>` Gerrit, no CI trigger), pass\n  as a new optional `standing_findings` workflow input, and\n  `merge_findings` appends those whose `norm_id` fresh Pass-1 did not produce. They reach\n  `code_review_verify_inputs` (`workflow_ops.py:270`); finders never see them.\n- **Shared kernel: no behaviour change.** `review_kernel.verify_instructions` (`verify.py:114`)\n  builds the listing and **plan-review also calls it** (`plan_review/passes.py:66`), so standing\n  wording is appended by a code-review-local wrapper in `code_review_verify_inputs` and in the\n  Pass-2 prompt `llm/reviewers/code-review-verify.md`; `verify.py` changes only the now-wrong\n  `prior_findings_block` docstring claim (`:435`) that the novelty sub-call is the only place prior\n  findings appear.\n- **Posture clamp (pinned, not assumed).** `pass3_decide` RECOMPUTES `decision` every run as \"BLOCK\n  iff blocking_enabled AND priority >= block_threshold\" (`decide.py:631`), threshold resolved per\n  criterion (`registry.py:535`), and on 1867 the defect changed criterion between patchsets — so\n  `code_review_decide` clamps a finding carrying `standing` to at most `standing.origin_decision`.\n  The floor is unaffected: a standing item matches a prior finding, so `rising_floor_drop`\n  (`:105`) sees low novelty and cannot drop it.\n\n\n## Scope\n\nNew: `llm/code_review/carry_forward.py` (cap-safe home for `STANDING_CAP`, the states,\n`standing_items()`, the wrapper text, the clamp — `workflow_ops.py` is 758 LOC vs the 800 cap) and\n`tests/unit/test_code_review_carry_forward.py` (flat layout — no `tests/unit/llm/`).\n\nEdited as above: `llm/code_review/sidecar.py`, `llm/code_review/workflow_ops.py`,\n`llm/workflow/gates/code-review.yaml`, `llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py`,\n`llm/reviewers/code-review-verify.md`, `llm/review_kernel/verify.py` (docstring only),\n`review_bot/adapter.py` (`_translate_findings` `:122` drops keys outside\n`{severity, dimension, detail, location}` — carry `standing`) and `review_bot/finding_publish.py`\n(`render_findings_block` `:126` / `build_inline_comments` `:147` render \"since patchset k\"; Gerrit\ntext is composed here, not in `adapter.py`).\n\n`tests/unit/test_code_review_region_gate.py` and `test_code_review_gate_session.py` stub the reader\n**by string**; add `revision` there or the floor reads a stale shape.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\nEach runs from the repo root and exits 0, incl. `python -c \"from\nrebar.llm.code_review.carry_forward import standing_items, STANDING_CAP\"`.\n\n- [ ] Ineligible prior items yield nothing (`dropped` bucket, empty `evidence`, no prior review): `pytest tests/unit/test_code_review_carry_forward.py -k ineligible -q`.\n\n- [ ] Each state's rule is pinned (incl. the unresolvable-region default) and carry is one-shot — an already-carried item classifies `withdrawn` and is not injected: `pytest tests/unit/test_code_review_carry_forward.py -k \"state_classification or withdrawn\" -q`.\n- [ ] A `still-present` item absent from fresh Pass-1 is injected carrying `standing.state` + `standing.origin_revision`: `pytest tests/unit/test_code_review_carry_forward.py -k merge_injects_standing -q`.\n- [ ] The reader exposes `revision`: `pytest tests/unit/test_code_review_artifact.py -k latest_code_review_result -q` with an added `revision` assertion.\n- [ ] Carry-forward never raises a posture, incl. over a `blocking_enabled` criterion past its `block_threshold`: `pytest tests/unit/test_code_review_carry_forward.py -k posture_clamp -q`.\n- [ ] The shared kernel is untouched beyond a docstring: `git diff origin/main -- src/rebar/llm/review_kernel/verify.py` shows docstring lines only; `pytest tests/unit/test_review_kernel.py tests/unit/test_plan_review_novelty.py -q`.\n- [ ] Gerrit marks carried findings and the Pass-2 prompt names them: `grep -c standing src/rebar/llm/reviewers/code-review-verify.md` and `grep -c \"since patchset\" src/rebar/review_bot/finding_publish.py` each return >= 1; `pytest tests/unit/test_review_bot.py -q`.\n- [ ] Convergence is not regressed: `pytest tests/unit/test_code_review_region_gate.py tests/unit/test_code_review_gate_session.py -q`.\n- [ ] Repo gates hold: `make lint` (it runs `check_complexity_baseline.py --check`, which must report no `new`/`increased`); every touched `src/rebar` file is within `.github/module-size-limit.txt`."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787376900231428001,"uuid":"1863f93f-4fc4-4c06-8ee4-b30febfbd4fb"}